# macOS
.DS_Store

# R session leftovers. Both copies in this repository are empty, but an
# .Rhistory records whatever was typed at the console, which on this project
# means paths and identifiers that must not be published. Ignore it by rule
# rather than relying on it staying empty.
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Environments
.env
.venv/
venv/

# Quarto transient render artifacts.
/.quarto/
*.knit.md
*_files/
*_cache/

# Rendered HTML reports. Derived artifacts, regenerable with `quarto render`,
# and not worth versioning: at ~4 MB each they are past GitHub's file-display
# limit, and GitHub shows raw source for .html rather than rendering it, so the
# committed copies could not be read on the site at all. The PDF renders of the
# same documents ARE committed and do preview inline, which is what the README
# points readers to. Render locally, or publish to Pages, if you want the HTML.
results_partA.html
results_partB.html
results_partC.html

# Leftover intermediate files from a PDF (xelatex) render that gets
# interrupted or run with a keep-tex-style option — none of these are ever
# a committed source in this repo, just build byproducts of results_partA.qmd
# / results_partB.qmd.
*.aux
*.log
*.toc
*.pdf.md
*.tex

# Presentation figures: derived artifacts regenerable with `python make_figs.py`.
# Not versioned so they can't go stale against the code that generates them —
# this already happened once (figures committed in e3683cc, then make_figs.py
# changed in 6b245ce without the committed PNGs being regenerated to match).
figures/

# Exception: images/figures/ IS versioned. The rule above was written for the
# repository-root figures/, but it matches any directory of that name, and the
# anatomy figure of Part C has to be committed — it cannot be regenerated from
# a clone, because it is drawn from DICOM that this repository cannot carry.
!images/figures/
!images/figures/**

# Imaging data pulled from PPMI: resting-state fMRI DICOM series (rsfMRI_LR)
# for 16 participants, plus the accompanying manifest. NEVER commit this.
#
#   * It is human subject data — 16 participants (8 Control, 8 PD) with sex,
#     age and clinical group in data.csv — and this repository is public.
#   * It is redistributed under a Data Use Agreement that does not permit
#     republication; the DUA is with the data provider, not with this project.
#   * It is ~150 MB across 3,652 files, far past what git should carry.
#
# Note this is the functional arm, which was not pursued: the T1 structural
# data behind Chapter 5 never lived here, it lives outside the repository in
# T1_data_def/ and deriv/.
#
# Anyone reproducing the images branch must request the data from the provider
# under their own agreement. Document the accession/query in the thesis instead.
data/

# ...but a bare `data/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, and
# funTDA/data/ holds the 17 GRN adjacency matrices that Part A reads. Those are
# public H3N2 network data, they are small, and results_partA.qmd cannot run
# without them. They survive today only because git ignores nothing already
# tracked — remove them from the index once and they could not be added back
# without -f, and a fresh clone would lose Part A silently. Hence the negation.
!funTDA/data/
!funTDA/data/**

# Surface-projected functional data for the images branch: per-subject BOLD
# timecourses on the fsaverage5 mesh (.func.gii), supplied by the supervisor.
# Same rule as data/ above — human subject data, public repository, NEVER
# commit it. Subject identifiers are in the filenames, so even the file listing
# is identifying. The fsaverage5 geometry these files are defined on is NOT
# subject data: it is a template, and it ships inside the `nilearn` package
# (nilearn.datasets.fetch_surf_fsaverage), so nothing here needs to carry it.
data_images/
*.func.gii

# Local reading copies of cited literature; not distributed with this repo.
references/

# Part C (images): the alias -> PPMI identifier mapping produced by
# images/export_for_repo.py. The exported diagrams and landscapes under
# images/output/ ARE committed — they are topological summaries two steps
# removed from the image and carry no identifier — but the file that maps
# sub-01 ... sub-16 back to the PPMI subject numbers must never be. NEVER
# commit this.
images/subject_map.csv

# FreeSurfer / FSL derivatives for Part C: several hundred MB of NIfTI, all
# regenerable from the DICOM by images/pipeline/. Not versioned.
images/deriv/

# Belt and braces. Every rule above excludes imaging data by PATH, which only
# works for the directories somebody thought of; deriv/ actually lives outside
# this repository, so images/deriv/ above is defensive already. These exclude
# by EXTENSION, so a stray volume dropped anywhere cannot be committed by
# accident. Nothing legitimate in this repository is a NIfTI or a DICOM: what
# Part C carries is the topological summary, which is CSV.
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.dcm
*.DCM
*.mgz
